<title>GUATEMALA: Proposed mining law heading to Guatemalan congress.</title>
<headline>Proposed mining law heading to Guatemalan congress.</headline>
<byline>Fiona Ortiz</byline>
<dateline>GUATEMALA CITY 1996-10-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Energy and Mines Ministry will present a bill to the Guatemalan Congress next week designed to attract foreign investment in mining, a government official said Friday.</p>
<p>&quot;The new law will open the doors to mining which has been asleep in Guatemala because we are proposing a law that is competitive at an international level and offers legal security,&quot; Mario Martinez, director of mines, told Reuters.</p>
</text>
